#. Translators: Keep CLI flags, argument values, and shortcut examples unchanged.
#: src/main.c:305
#, c-format
msgid ""
"Usage: %s [OPTIONS] [IMAGE|VIDEO|-|--stdin]\n"
"\n"
"  --name NAME                             Name for an image or video read "
"from stdin\n"
"  --save-path PATH                        Where Save puts an image read from "
"stdin,\n"
"                                          without asking. PATH includes the "
"file\n"
"                                          name, its extension picks the "
"format,\n"
"                                          and a file already there is "
"overwritten\n"
"  --screenshot [area|screen]              Take a screenshot, of an area "
"unless told\n"
"                                          otherwise. Opens the editor unless "
"that's\n"
"                                          turned off in Preferences\n"
"  --record [area|screen|window]           Record the screen, an area unless "
"told\n"
"                                          otherwise. Run it again while "
"recording\n"
"                                          to stop. Opens the editor unless "
"that's\n"
"                                          turned off in Preferences\n"
"  --screen NAME                           With --screenshot or --record: use "
"this\n"
"                                          screen, e.g. DP-1. Doesn't support "
"GNOME\n"
"  --notify                                Use with --screenshot or --record. "
"Shows\n"
"                                          a notification after the capture "
"that\n"
"                                          lets you edit it, instead of "
"opening the\n"
"                                          editor. Saves and copies as set "
"in\n"
"                                          Preferences\n"
"  --gapplication-service                  Run as a background application "
"service\n"
"  --delay SECONDS                         With --screenshot: wait this many "
"whole\n"
"                                          seconds first, at most 300. With --"
"record:\n"
"                                          count down this long before "
"recording\n"
"  --close-on-copy, --no-close-on-copy     Override the \"Close on copy\" "
"preference\n"
"  --close-window-shortcut SHORTCUT        Override a shortcut for this "
"launch\n"
"  --copy-shortcut SHORTCUT\n"
"  --copy-without-closing-shortcut SHORTCUT\n"
"  --save-shortcut SHORTCUT\n"
"  --save-and-close-shortcut SHORTCUT\n"
"  --save-copy-and-close-shortcut SHORTCUT\n"
"  --screenshot-area-shortcut SHORTCUT\n"
"  --screenshot-screen-shortcut SHORTCUT\n"
"\n"
"SHORTCUT is a key, or modifiers and a key joined with \"+\", for example\n"
"\"s\", \"F5\", \"escape\", \"ctrl+s\" or \"ctrl+shift+s\". It can also be\n"
"\"right-click\", a tablet button such as \"tablet-button-1\", or \"none\" "
"to\n"
"unassign. Modifiers are ctrl, shift, alt and super. Overrides last for this\n"
"launch only.\n"
msgstr ""
"Utilisation : %s [OPTIONS] [IMAGE|VIDEO|-|--stdin]\n"
"\n"
"  --name NOM                               Nomme l’image ou la vidéo lue "
"depuis\n"
"                                           l’entrée standard\n"
"  --save-path CHEMIN                       Enregistre l’image lue depuis "
"l’entrée\n"
"                                           standard à cet emplacement sans "
"demander.\n"
"                                           Incluez le nom du fichier : son "
"extension\n"
"                                           détermine le format. Si le "
"fichier existe,\n"
"                                           il est remplacé\n"
"  --screenshot [area|screen]               Capture une zone par défaut. "
"Ouvre l’éditeur\n"
"                                           sauf si l’option est désactivée "
"dans les\n"
"                                           préférences\n"
"  --record [area|screen|window]            Enregistre une zone par défaut. "
"Relancez\n"
"                                           la commande pour arrêter. Ouvre "
"l’éditeur\n"
"                                           sauf si l’option est désactivée "
"dans les\n"
"                                           préférences\n"
"  --screen NOM                             Avec --screenshot ou --record : "
"utilise cet\n"
"                                           écran, par ex. DP-1. Non pris en "
"charge\n"
"                                           sous GNOME\n"
"  --notify                                 Avec --screenshot ou --record : "
"affiche une\n"
"                                           notification pour modifier la "
"capture au\n"
"                                           lieu d’ouvrir l’éditeur. "
"L’enregistrement\n"
"                                           et la copie suivent les "
"préférences\n"
"  --gapplication-service                   Lance l’application en arrière-"
"plan\n"
"  --delay SECONDES                         Avec --screenshot : attend ce "
"nombre entier\n"
"                                           de secondes (300 au maximum). "
"Avec --record :\n"
"                                           lance un compte à rebours de "
"cette durée\n"
"  --close-on-copy, --no-close-on-copy      Remplace la préférence « Fermer "
"après la copie »\n"
"  --close-window-shortcut RACCOURCI        Remplace un raccourci pour ce "
"lancement\n"
"  --copy-shortcut RACCOURCI\n"
"  --copy-without-closing-shortcut RACCOURCI\n"
"  --save-shortcut RACCOURCI\n"
"  --save-and-close-shortcut RACCOURCI\n"
"  --save-copy-and-close-shortcut RACCOURCI\n"
"  --screenshot-area-shortcut RACCOURCI\n"
"  --screenshot-screen-shortcut RACCOURCI\n"
"\n"
"RACCOURCI désigne une touche, éventuellement précédée de modificateurs\n"
"séparés par « + », par exemple \"s\", \"F5\", \"escape\", \"ctrl+s\" ou "
"\"ctrl+shift+s\".\n"
"Il peut aussi valoir \"right-click\", un bouton de tablette comme\n"
"\"tablet-button-1\", ou \"none\" pour désactiver le raccourci. Les "
"modificateurs\n"
"sont ctrl, shift, alt et super. Ces réglages ne valent que pour ce "
"lancement.\n"

